# Netlify / Cloudflare Pages redirect rules.
# (Apache hosts use .htaccess instead; see DEPLOY.md.)
#
# This map is preserved SEO and survives every rebuild. Two generations of
# URL now point here: the original Sitejet site, and the hand-built site
# that replaced it. Deleting a line here silently discards whatever ranking
# and inbound links that URL had.

# --- Portuguese -------------------------------------------------------------
# /pt/ is a REAL section again, so the old blanket "/pt/* -> /" rule is gone.
# It used to 301 every Portuguese URL to the English home page, which threw
# away the Brazilian-market SEO the Sitejet site had built. /pt/sobre-nos in
# particular now resolves to the actual Portuguese About page, at the same
# URL it had before.
#
# Nothing to declare here: /pt, /pt/sobre-nos, /pt/servicos, /pt/trabalhos,
# /pt/contato, /pt/aviso-legal and /pt/privacidade are all served directly.

# --- Legacy Sitejet URLs (301) ----------------------------------------------
/en               /            301
/en/*             /:splat      301

# --- Pages the rebuild renamed or merged (301) ------------------------------
/about-us                    /about       301
/our-work                    /work        301
/web-design-development      /services    301
# The three-tier pricing ladder is gone — it advertised EUR 0 across all
# three tiers and "Placeholder feature" bullets. Services is the honest
# destination for anyone who arrives looking for it.
/pricing                     /services    301

# --- Strip .html so canonical extensionless URLs are the only public form ---
/index.html       /                        301
/*.html           /:splat                  301
